Verification: a real format-1 RocksDB checkpoint image is opened through `RocksDB.openReadOnly`. The physical inspector enforces finite file/byte bounds, exact column-family inventory, empty default column family with checked iterator status, manifest file length/checksum equality, and exact Store format/Shard/db identity/incarnation, checkpoint ID, applied source position, and mutation sequence. The state inventory scans every registered Column Family under finite record/byte/time bounds; it counts key-kind prefixes and decodes old Message status and retired identity records, checking each Message key/source route belongs to the checkpoint Shard. The manifest-bound physical inventory is checked before and after the logical scan. Tests cover SCHEDULED status inventory, malformed Message rejection without file changes, read-budget exhaustion, and a manifest/image mismatch.

